As several players have said recently, Nethack is a little dull when
you realize that virtually everything you need for the standard AK is
handed to you.

Here's a list of ideas that have occured to me over the past couple
weeks of playing that might make NetHack a little more interesting and
challenging without greatly altering the game from its roots.

1. The gnomish mines is NOT guaranteed in every game. (70% chance that
it exists) This makes the protection racket more of a calculated
gamble. It also potentially eliminates the guaranteed luckstone and
lighting shop in the game.

Alternative: to spice things up, an alternative to the gnomish mines
could be created (orc/goblin city?). It would alter the game more and
would require more work, however, it might be fun to play with
different ideas here. Different items would be available in the city vs
the mines.

2. Sokoban is NOT guaranteed in every game (40% chance that it exists).
Potentially eliminates the guaranteed BoH/AoR from the game. Caching
becomes an even more important skill

Alternative: more levels. I enjoyed Sokoban, but after beating it for
the n-teenth time it is dull, dull, dull. more levels would freshen
things up a bit. Again a lot more work.

3. Wand of Wishing is NOT guaranteed at the castle. Wishes are nice,
but at the point you get this wand of wishing  it's either far too
useful (i.e. you pretty much know what you're lacking and you can wish
for it) or it's pretty much unnecessary ("ho-hum I found most of my kit
already what else can I wish for?").

Alternative: It'd be better, in my opinion, if you really wanted to
have a guaranteed wand of wishing to include it early in the game, when
the players can be torn between whether they need to use it or whether
they should hold off. Perhaps the Oracle has a guaranteed Wand of
Wishing on her exalted person? ;)

4. Wands of Wishing cannot be recharged, period. Only got one charge?
Well, it IS a wish after all. Wishes don't grow on trees you know.

5. AoLS or BoWW in Vlad's tower, but never both. Sometimes neither.

6. When stepping onto a space with a cross-aligned altar you are
occasionally blasted with its power, much like picking up a
cross-aligned artifact.

7. Wishing for a quest artifact automatically summons the corresponding
quest nemesis who may or may not be generated holding/weilding the item
in question. (go on, wish for those eyes of the overworld, if you dare)
Only works once for each nemesis.

Implementing most of these, I think, would break bones files, but I
think they would make Nethack a lot more "think on your feet" that it
is now. The beauty of NetHack is there are so many solutions to
complicated problems, but I think the current method of guaranteeing
items makes us a bit too complacent. By simply removing some of those
absolutes, it forces the player to reexamine his or her situation, It
makes wishes even more important ("the blessed staff of scallops, or
the 7 blessed candles I need to finish the game, hmmm....").

It might even make the game unbeatable at times, but I see nothing
wrong with that. I think pulling off a victory by the skin of one's
teeth or even going down in a blaze of glory is a far more satisfying
result than Yet Another Perfect Ascension Kit.


